author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: A changed blocker invalidates acknowledgment; two receivers do not overwrite each other; missing required evidence stays visible; typed SDK and CLI with compact TOON/JSON and actionable refusals; non-git public-tracker validation; npm and Bun release gates at unchanged thresholds
comments[26]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-21T18:40:49.216Z",codex-agent,"Overlap check: core CLI 2026.10.21 claims manage ownership; brief prompt and since emit prose/deltas; pm-memory stores standing knowledge; pm-context context-handoff/context-usage tracks served facts, not receipt-based understanding. Checked pm-context open PRs: only dependency PR #162, no since-delta PR currently. Coordinate with its since-delta work without implementing history delta here. Acceptance criteria recorded on this new item. Design: immutable revision-bound contracts, independent append-only receiver receipts, live stale/evidence assessment, native SDK storage without git."
  "2026-10-21T18:47:14.450Z",codex-agent,"Implemented typed packet/response/refusal SDK and structured create, preview, ack and show commands. Native Decision bodies hold immutable contracts; lock-scoped idempotent comment appends isolate receivers. Full item content digests include transitive declared blockers and inverse blocks edges. Live status retains missing required links. Added README and JSON example; building no-git, concurrent-process, integrity and budget regressions."
  "2026-10-21T18:51:09.213Z",codex-agent,"Coordination refreshed: pm-context has an active feat/since-delta-pack candidate at 6ed5991, with context-pack since --from/--cursor, ranked changes and omission receipts; no PR is open yet. README explicitly references that candidate and assigns delta/cursor ownership there. Real-data validation: public origin/main tracker, 86 items, 5 read-only previews, 5 revision rows, all 5 synthetic required links remained missing; compact JSON 798-876 bytes (4159 total), conservative ceiling 611-650 tokens, median 4445ms and maximum 5225ms under shared-host load. All 179 copied public files remained hash-identical; snapshot was read-only and outside git."
  "2026-10-21T18:58:17.316Z",codex-agent,"Real CLI no-git validation passed: create, preview, concurrent acknowledgments from two independent processes, receiver filtering and native TOON/JSON output. Added machine-readable handoff refusal codes and remedies. Public-data measurements are recorded in docs/handoff-validation.md. Existing release thresholds remain unchanged; final exact-source gates and behavioral revert proof are still pending."
  "2026-10-21T19:04:17.401Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: in a disposable non-git source copy, changed only staleItems to return an empty list. The dedicated changed-blocker regression failed with an AssertionError: actual [] versus the changed blocker id. The package source was untouched. Earlier contention-only failure was rejected as insufficient proof. Added bounded native lock retries for certified reads and idempotent appends; creates never auto-retry."
  "2026-10-21T19:08:02.275Z",codex-agent,"Supplemental local strict health: history_drift passes, stale work is advisory, and shared-clone merge_fence_drift is gate-failing after generated install changes were excluded from this feature. No merge configuration or receipt repair was attempted under the no-git scope rule. Fresh CI installs its own native setup; this local operational finding is separate from the feature and release checks."
  "2026-10-21T19:11:57.753Z",codex-agent,"Tracked focused run exposed an invalid test assumption: certified reads can succeed while a native item lock is held. Replaced that assertion with a real locked receipt append, verified its typed refusal, then released the lock and verified idempotent retry. Targeted exhausted-lock and filesystem append-refusal regressions both pass; no SDK mocks. The implementation did not need a behavior change for this test correction."
  "2026-10-21T19:23:44.461Z",codex-agent,"Current tracked feature suite passes: 14 tests, 0 failures, 0 skips. handoff.ts coverage is 100% lines, 99.15% branches and 100% functions. Ran through pm test --run --progress with the linked focused command. Also verified a strict NodeNext TypeScript consumer can import the emitted SDK declarations and assign all four public function signatures. npm and Bun full release gates are running independently against source-identical commit 4d7827f; draft PR #166 is open for exact-head CI."
  "2026-10-21T19:30:48.627Z",codex-agent,"Exact-head CI at 4d7827f passes: Node 22 and Node 26 each report 404 tests passed, zero failures/skips. Aggregate coverage is 100/98.28/100 on Node 22 and 100/98.32/100 on Node 26 (lines/branches/functions), with both shipped source files measured. All three packed scenarios pass: npm/current SDK 2026.10.17, Bun/current SDK 2026.10.17, npm/minimum SDK 2026.10.13; each retains two receivers and the missing evidence requirement. Fresh CI strict health and Windows audits pass. PR #166 is ready for review; full local npm/Bun runs continue."
  "2026-10-21T19:38:49.341Z",codex-agent,"Addressed the scoped PR documentation finding: the creation example now uses pm brief handoff create, consistent with preview/ack/show. Runtime source and tests are unchanged. Independent automated review remains unavailable: Greptile trial ended, CodeRabbit skipped automatic review under its repository policy, and Sourcery exhausted its weekly budget. Their statuses are missing review evidence, not approval. No bot mentions or billing/configuration changes were made."
  "2026-10-21T19:42:30.621Z",codex-agent,Created deduplicated follow-up pm-brief-1oo2 for unavailable independent PR reviews; it is open and unclaimed for an owner-approved resolution. The requested feature remains scoped to handoff contracts. Documentation correction and gate/review receipts will be pushed together; no runtime source changed after 4d7827f.
  "2026-10-21T19:49:59.992Z",codex-agent,Boundary validation found and reproduced a fresh-packet read failure for a legitimate native item title of 2121 characters. Native metadata titles were incorrectly revalidated with the 2000-character obligation-input cap. The reader now preserves native title/status text under the aggregate packet budget while retaining obligation input caps. Added a real-tracker long-title round-trip regression; preliminary local full gates were canceled so final gates can run on the corrected source. Prior 404-test CI remains scoped to the earlier head.
  "2026-10-21T19:53:30.814Z",codex-agent,"The long-title correction passes the real-tracker round-trip regression and the existing invalid-input cases (2/2). Behavioral revert proof: in a disposable source copy, changed only string validation back to its fixed 2000-character cap while preserving the signature; the new long-title test fails with the expected integrity refusal. The corrected implementation preserves full native titles, and obligation size limits remain enforced and documented."
  "2026-10-21T20:05:31.610Z",codex-agent,"Extended the same boundary correction to native identifiers after reproducing a fresh-packet failure with a 168-character blocker reference and confirming the SDK accepts 159-character item ids. Obligation/actor keys retain their 128-character cap; native focus ids, evidence item ids, packet ids and snapshot references retain full safe identifier length under the aggregate budget. Construction validates the same native snapshot fields as reads. Native title, native-id/reference and invalid-input regressions now pass 3/3. Additional packed npm/Bun acceptance against CLI 2026.10.21 passed on the earlier normal-sized packet cohort; final-source gates are being refreshed."
  "2026-10-21T20:20:36.712Z",codex-agent,"Final runtime source c55c13b passes exact-head CI on Node 22 and 26: 406/406 tests, zero skipped, aggregate 100% lines / 98.28% branches / 100% functions across both shipped source files. The linked native-boundary PM command passes 2/2. Native-id behavioral revert also fails as expected when only key validation is restored to a fixed 128-character cap. Refreshed packed npm and Bun acceptance against CLI 2026.10.21 passes on c55c13b; each retains two receivers and missing evidence. Default SDK 2026.10.17 and minimum SDK 2026.10.13 packed matrices also pass in CI. Full local npm/Bun release commands continue."
  "2026-10-21T20:29:24.166Z",codex-agent,"Final-source read-only validation refreshed at c55c13b with git absent from PATH and the process cwd outside git: 86 certified items, 5 packets, 5 revision rows, all 5 missing requirements retained, JSON 798-876 bytes (4159 total), conservative ceilings 611-650 tokens. Median/max generation measured 658/1290ms. All 179 original snapshot files remained hash-identical; docs/handoff-validation.md now records these final-source measurements."
  "2026-10-21T20:32:26.544Z",codex-agent,"Coordination refresh: pm-context since-delta work is now open as PR #164 (https://github.com/unbraind/pm-context/pull/164). README and PR text link it directly. It owns cursor-based delta selection and resume/omission semantics; pm-brief owns immutable contracts, per-receiver acknowledgments and current revision/evidence assessment. No sibling files or tracker records were modified."
  "2026-10-21T20:48:38.229Z",codex-agent,"Final verification complete for runtime source c55c13b: npm run release:check passes with isolated Git identity and 406/406 tests, zero skipped, 100/98.28/100 aggregate lines/branches/functions; bun run release:check passes in an isolated source-identical checkout with 406/406 tests, zero skipped, 100/98.33/100. Both complete audits, packed npm/Bun/current/minimum-host acceptance, changelog checks and publish attestation. Exact-head Node 22/26 CI also passes 406/406 and 100/98.28/100. Final-source CLI 2026.10.21 npm/Bun packed acceptance passes separately. All three behavioral revert proofs fail as intended. No upstream CLI/SDK defect was identified; native length handling defects were in pm-brief and are fixed. Independent review availability remains open in pm-brief-1oo2. PR #166 remains unmerged and unreleased; this item remains open for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-10-22T12:08:49.490Z",codex-agent,"Review round for PR #166: pulled remote head 133a611; origin/main is already an ancestor. Retrieved all review threads and comments (one unresolved: PRRT_kwDOSzIO-c6u_RLd); latest CodeRabbit review has no outside-diff findings. Valid finding: locale collation equates distinct Unicode property names, making content digests depend on insertion order. Plan: use code-unit property ordering in implementation and signing helper, add real non-git tracker regression with behavioral revert proof, self-review the entire diff for related digest ordering defects, run unchanged npm and Bun release gates, commit tracker evidence and push without interacting with threads."
  "2026-10-22T12:13:29.432Z",codex-agent,"PR #166 fix and behavioral revert proof: canonical() and the independent test signing helper now order property keys by UTF-16 code units. New real SDK-initialized non-git tracker regression persists composed and decomposed Unicode keys in a declared object field, changes only their storage insertion order, verifies equal item revisions, valid/ready receipts and idempotent retry, then verifies a value mutation invalidates the receipt. Focused command node --test --test-name-pattern=\"Unicode key insertion\" test/handoff.test.ts passes 1/1 with zero skips. In a disposable source copy, reverted only the production canonical comparator to localeCompare; the same regression fails 0/1 with ERR_ASSERTION at the revision equality check (different hashes). The fixed test helper remained unchanged in that proof. Whole-PR review checked all digest/signing paths, blocker ordering, CLI transport, packing and documentation; no additional instance of this defect class found. Fixed-field packet document ordering is unaffected; older item digests with differently ordered custom properties can conservatively require a fresh handoff. npm ci passed with zero vulnerabilities. Full unchanged npm/Bun release gates follow."
  "2026-10-22T12:46:16.766Z",codex-agent,"PR #166 final review-round validation: npm run release:check passed in the package worktree with isolated Git identity, 407/407 tests, zero failures/skips/cancellations/todos, aggregate lines/branches/functions 100/98.28/100 across both shipped source files; bun run release:check passed the same 407/407 and 100/98.33/100 in an independently verified source-identical disposable checkout with isolated Git identity. Both passed all three packed consumers (npm/current host 2026.10.17, Bun/current 2026.10.17, npm/minimum 2026.10.13), zero production audit vulnerabilities, docstrings (147 declarations), changelog and publish attestation. Coverage thresholds remain 100/97.85/100. Initial test compilation found ES2023 array syntax and custom-field excess-property fixture typing; corrected without changing production behavior or thresholds, and the full gate passed on retry. No runtime timeout occurred. Repeated comparator-only behavioral revert against the final test source fails 0/1 at revision equality; fixed focused regression passes directly and via pm test (1/1 linked command). dist is rebuilt by both gates and is not tracked. No new pm CLI/SDK bug established. Review finding PRRT_kwDOSzIO-c6u_RLd is fixed; thread interaction, merge and release remain excluded. Keep this item in progress for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-10-22T15:15:24.416Z",codex-agent,"Review round 2 for PR #166: remote head 68c7903 is current and origin/main is already an ancestor. The prior Unicode-order thread is now resolved by the reviewer; one new unresolved thread PRRT_kwDOSzIO-c6vPcPE flags permission-denial tests on Windows/root. Latest CodeRabbit review has no outside-diff findings. Verify and fix that test portability issue with a behavioral regression, inspect the changed code for the DeepScan commit status reporting one new issue, run unchanged npm and Bun release gates and record all evidence before pushing. Previously completed PR #165 remains untouched. Git tree inspection confirms dist is ignored and has no committed entries on this branch; rebuild emitted output without adding generated artifacts."
  "2026-10-22T15:20:01.804Z",codex-agent,"Round 2 fixes: verified CodeRabbit thread PRRT_kwDOSzIO-c6vPcPE against both permission-based failure fixtures. Replaced chmod-based directory denial with a scoped regular file obstructing the native history directory; real item reads still work, real create/append mutations refuse with the expected CLI/SDK remedies, and finally restores original history. Added recovery assertions proving create and append succeed after restoration; no skipped tests or SDK mocks. Focused native-failure and Unicode regressions pass 3/3 through the linked PM runner. Behavioral revert in a disposable copy changed only withBlockedHistory to execute its callback without blocking storage (the previous effective behavior when mode checks are bypassed): both refusal regressions fail with Missing expected rejection, 0/2. This is a test-fixture revert, not a production-function change; direct Windows/root execution is unavailable. DeepScan public issue 238141298 identifies MISMATCHED_TYPE_OF_ARG at test/handoff.test.ts:83, where an optional payload was cast into Object.keys. Replaced the cast with explicit row/object guards before Object.keys; the existing real-tracker Unicode regression covers the path. Whole-PR review found both chmod fixtures and no additional optional-to-Object.keys cast in changed code. Runtime source and dependency pins are unchanged. dist has no tracked entries and is rebuilt locally; generated artifacts remain ignored. Full npm/Bun gates follow, with remote DeepScan status verification required after push."
  "2026-10-22T15:50:04.616Z",codex-agent,"Round 2 full validation completed on identical runtime/test files: npm run release:check passed 407/407 tests, zero fail/skip/cancel/todo, aggregate lines/branches/functions 100/98.28/100 across both shipped source files; bun run release:check passed 407/407 with zero fail/skip/cancel/todo and 100/98.33/100 in an independently byte-verified source-identical checkout. Both passed three packed scenarios (npm/current, Bun/current, npm/minimum host), zero production vulnerabilities, 147 documented declarations, changelog and publish attestation at unchanged thresholds 100/97.85/100. Neither run had a timeout. Focused linked regressions passed 3/3; behavioral fixture revert fails both native refusal regressions 0/2, and original history remains append-only. DeepScan issue 238141298 is a conservative diagnostic: the prior deepEqual assertion already rejects a missing payload and TypeScript models that narrowing, so a compiler probe removing only the explicit guard did not fail and is not counted as a revert proof. Explicit row/object control-flow guards now remove the optional cast, with the real Unicode regression retained. No new production behavior or SDK defect is claimed. Remote DeepScan verification remains pending until this code is pushed; its exact commit/status receipt will be recorded separately. Direct Windows/root execution is unavailable; the regular-file obstruction avoids permission semantics without skips. No committed dist entries exist; builds regenerate ignored artifacts."
  "2026-10-22T15:51:30.954Z",codex-agent,"Round 2 remote validation receipt: pushed code/test commit 02e020ee4538a17f16c764fc836958915ac592b7. GitHub commit-status API reports DeepScan=success with description 0 new and 0 fixed issues; public analysis: https://deepscan.io/dashboard/#view=project&tid=30234&pid=32094&bid=1043831&subview=pull-request&prid=2496461. This clears the previous one-new-issue failure at 68c7903. Runtime/test files are byte-identical to those passed by both 407-test full release gates. No thread reply or resolution was made; PRRT_kwDOSzIO-c6vPcPE remains unresolved as instructed even though its portable failure-fixture fix is pushed. CodeRabbit latest commit status skips review and requests manual review; that is missing independent review evidence, not approval, and the existing availability follow-up remains applicable. This receipt update changes tracker evidence only; final head status will be verified again after push. No new pm CLI/SDK defect established."
  "2026-10-23T15:27:07.156Z",codex-agent,"DELIVERED: merged PR #166 (fefa1c6d903ce46459f261e3b3b63fb64f458aa3) is an ancestor of audited main 7172186062a0398ffe585a593f7636a84b847671. Inspected on main: test/handoff.test.ts, docs/handoff-validation.md. Changed blockers invalidate acknowledgments, independent receivers preserve histories, missing evidence stays visible, and bounded native gitless SDK/CLI/public-copy and unchanged npm/Bun gates are delivered. This tracker audit inspected existing tests/files; it does not claim a new full product test run."
